      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T23:13:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way I had pictured the interface in my head, I just wanted to wholesale send the focus state. This way, we could react to other changes in the future if we wanted to. Otherwise, it feel like a very specific hack, instead of something that could prove useful in the future (i.e. we could use focus state as a proxy for stream state and show paused/stopped INSTEAD of playing if we don\u0027t also have an audio stream coming out the speakers).\n\nI would also argue that AvrcpControllerStateMachine shouldn\u0027t really know _anything_ about the implementation details around how BluetoothMediaBrowserService uses the focus state. Its a separation of responsibilities thing.\n\nYou could argue the YAGNI principle too though, but I fall on the other side of the fence for this one in particular.",
      "parentUuid": "4706b475_cbe22098",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 506,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 506,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "d0981ed786456448ad9ba3622e2dfd3f361dd7a5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
