      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T21:28:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there any forbidden `currentState`s where we do *not* want to signal a temporary \"Connecting\" state, e.g., `STATE_ERROR`? E.g.,\n```\nif (currentState \u003d\u003d null\n        || currentState.getState() \u003d\u003d PlaybackStateCompat.STATE_ERROR) {\n    Log.w(\n            TAG,\n            \"onAudioFocusStateChanged(state\u003d\"\n                    + state\n                    + \"): current playback state is \"\n                    + currentState);\n    return;\n}\n\nPlaybackStateCompat connectingState \u003d\n        new PlaybackStateCompat.Builder(currentState)\n                .setState(\n                        PlaybackStateCompat.STATE_CONNECTING,\n                        currentState.getPosition(),\n                        currentState.getPlaybackSpeed())\n                .build();\nservice.mSession.setPlaybackState(connectingState);\nservice.mSession.setPlaybackState(currentState);\n```",
